10. Commercial Attribution.

  (a) Definitions for this section.

      "Commercial Use" means any use of the Work or a Derivative Work that is
      primarily intended for or directed toward commercial advantage or
      monetary compensation. This includes, for example, incorporating the Work
      or a Derivative Work into a product or service that is sold, licensed for
      a fee, or offered as a paid or monetized service, or using it internally
      to provide a service to paying customers.

      "Non-Commercial Use" means use that is not a Commercial Use, such as
      personal use, use for research, use in a non-profit activity, and use in
      academic teaching, in each case where the use is not primarily intended
      for or directed toward commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

      "Redistribution" means providing the Work or a Derivative Work, in Source
      or Object form, to a third party.

      "Modification" means any change to the Work, including wrapping,
      integrating, adapting, translating, renaming, forking, or incorporating
      it into a larger system.

      "Attribution" means a reasonably visible written credit that clearly
      identifies both the name "Cicero" and "Emil Valiyev" as the original
      author/developer.

  (b) Condition. If You make Commercial Use of the Work or a Derivative Work,
      then, in addition to all other conditions of this License, You must
      provide Attribution.

  (c) Form. The Attribution must be substantially equivalent to:

          Uses Cicero — originally developed by Emil Valiyev.

      You may adapt the wording, but it must clearly identify "Cicero" and
      "Emil Valiyev".

  (d) Location. The Attribution may appear in any reasonably accessible
      location associated with the Commercial Use or with the product or
      service in which the Work or a Derivative Work is used. Examples include
      documentation, an acknowledgements or credits section, an About or
      Credits page, a public repository README, or a comparable attribution
      location.

  (e) No visual requirements. This section requires only attribution. It does
      not impose any requirement about logos, colors, fonts, size, placement,
      or promotional wording.

  (f) Modification and integration. Modification, wrapping, integration,
      renaming, forking, or incorporation of the Work into a larger system does
      not by itself remove the obligation in paragraph (b) where this License
      otherwise applies to the resulting use.

  (g) Non-Commercial Use. Non-Commercial Use is not subject to the obligation
      in paragraph (b). All other terms of this License continue to apply.

  (h) Delimitation. This section adds an attribution condition for Commercial
      Use. It does not restrict the permissions granted in Sections 2 and 3 and
      does not add any other restriction, fee, or permission requirement.


